menu "Ark EPD diagnostics"

    config ARK_EPD_ABC_DIAG
        bool "Enable experimental ColorQual A/B/C RAM diagnostic"
        default n
        help
            Laboratory firmware only. Interpret the first native Format2 body
            byte as (diagnostic_mode << 3) | B. Modes: 0=reuse A, 1=rewrite A,
            2=write constant B before the second Qual refresh. Reject modes >2.
            Always full-clear before the original three Qual refreshes. LUTs,
            registers and REF count are identical between diagnostic modes;
            modes 1/2 add one RAM transfer slot, so total timing is NOT fixed.
            Ordinary Format2 pictures are not suitable diagnostic inputs.
            Also accept private lab Format 0x7F, reserved bytes 12..15 ABC9,
            exactly one 720x480 frame of little-endian uint16 pixels 0..511.
            Bits 8..6=A, 5..3=B, 2..0=C drive the original three Qual phases
            with a RAM-only write per phase, after the same full clear.
            Invalid high bits are rejected before any clear or refresh.
            No new public film format or BLE command is introduced.

    config ARK_EPD_PROFILE
        bool "Enable per-frame driver timing"
        default n
        help
            Emit one ESP_LOGI EPD_PROFILE JSON record per mono or 8bpp display
            driver call. Keep the ESP-IDF log level at Info or higher to see it.
            All timings use microseconds; this is not end-to-end FPS.
            Stages include preparation passes and original command/wait/delay
            time. RAM timing includes encoding and SPI transfer. This option
            does not modify LUTs, SPI frequency, panel timings or recovery.

endmenu
